The Mind's standing context in every turn, and brains that provision themselves.

`turn_context_for_agent` on the `Memory` trait (default empty) lets a backend put
its own standing context ahead of the recalled entries; `AgentScopedMemory`
(the bound agent's, never a sibling's), `ScannedMemory` (the read-time scan),
`AuditedMemory` and `RetrievalPipeline` (never cached) forward it, and
`render_memory_context` opens the `[Memory context]` block with it, charged to
the block's budget, so it is re-rendered every turn, stripped from history
like the rest of the preamble, and outlives context compaction.
`XanimaStorageConfig` gains `turn_context`, `turn_context_max_chars` and
`provision_token_file`. The backend that fills all this in is the overlay's
crates/caelza-memory/src/xanima.rs (brain_turn_context, brain_provision_agent).

